[case_guidance] case_id | kind | ordinal | item
"C-6e85826d00" | "avoid" | 0 | "Adding wrapper objects, broad visitor protocols, or no-op methods solely to clear the finding without improving cohesion or reducing coupling."
"C-6e85826d00" | "avoid" | 1 | "Moving each decision into a differently named helper while retaining the repeated variant knowledge."
"C-6e85826d00" | "avoid" | 2 | "Replacing switches with equivalent if/else chains."
"C-6e85826d00" | "avoid" | 3 | "Introducing an interface while callers still select concrete implementations repeatedly."
"C-6e85826d00" | "avoid" | 4 | "Renaming constants, aliases, variables, or files solely to evade correlation."
"C-6e85826d00" | "lead" | 0 | "Examine whether callers can send the same message to interchangeable role players instead of selecting behavior themselves."
"C-6e85826d00" | "lead" | 1 | "If the variants select implementations, use a factory or construction boundary to select once and return a common behavioral role; callers then send messages through that role."
"C-6e85826d00" | "lead" | 2 | "If independent operations inspect the same variants, evaluate a visitor or adapter with one dispatch boundary; keep operation-specific behavior, traversal policy, and results with each operation."
"C-6e85826d00" | "lead" | 3 | "If branches merely map variants to data, consider a data-driven representation owned near the variant definition."
"C-6e85826d00" | "lead" | 4 | "Move behavior toward the object or role that has the knowledge required to perform it."
